== A Saint of the Order of a Day Put to Rest

#poem[][

I am St. James. I hold my head in my hands\
Not my heart like St. Augustine\
I can still see; though my thought's disconnected\
Not like Lucy with a plate of her eyes\
Jerome has his skin draped over his arm\
Can't imagine how cold he must be\
None of have lost how we suffered\
And like our sundry forms,\
when you go away \
someone remembers\
a statue of you that you were at that moment

I am St. James. I hold my head in my hands\
I am a thousand faces in a thousand illustrations\
In all kinds of colours and multiple dimensions\
Your sculpture changes as you travel your intentions

I hope you carry a book or a lily\
A sheaf of wheat or a plough or a lamp\
Maybe a skateboard some chalk or a handful of Lego

